    "sentence_translations": [
      "Ben’s Diary—Is Anything Wrong?",
      "",
      "I am staying in a hotel today. I remember the teacher said: “‘Shi’ means ‘room’.”",
      "",
      "I walked into the hotel and asked the receptionist, “Excuse me, do you have any ‘rooms’?”",
      "",
      "The receptionist looked at me weirdly and said, “We’re fine. Is something wrong?”",
      "",
      "I thought to myself: Why would they ask me if I “had any ‘rooms’”?",
      "I don’t own the hotel, why would I “have ‘rooms’”?",
      "",
      "I felt that she didn’t understand what I meant, so I said, “I want to stay at the hotel.”",
      "",
      "This time it seemed that the receptionist understood me; she said:",
      "“Okay. What type of room do you want to stay in?”",
      "",
      "Later, I told Lili about this incident. Lili laughed and said:",
      "“You can’t ask ‘do you still have rooms (shi),’ you need to ask ’do you still have rooms (fangjian).’”",
      "Even though “shi” does mean “room,” it often needs to be used in conjunction with other words.",
      "Like in office, classroom, lounge…”"
    ]
  }
